[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Back in the Old Country]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.27]Lesson 57 | 第57课
[00:02.30]Back in the old country | 重返故里
[00:09.57]Did the narrater find his mother's grave? | 叙述者找到他母亲的坟墓了吗？
[00:13.98]I stopped to let the car cool off and to study the map. | 我停下车，让发动机冷却一下，同时查看一下地图。
[00:18.28]I had expected to be near my objective by now, but everything still seemed alien to me. | 我原以为此时快到目的地了，但周围的一切对我来说仍很陌生。
[00:25.73]I was only five when my father had taken me abroad, and that was eighteen years ago. | 我5岁时父亲便带我出了国，那是18年前的事了。
[00:32.35]When my mother had died after a tragic accident, he did not quickly recover from the shock and loneliness. | 母亲在一次意外的事故中死去后，父亲未能很快从震惊与孤独中恢复过来。
[00:40.37]Everything around him was full of her presence, continually reopening the wound. | 他周围的一切处处都有母亲的影子，不断地揭开这个创伤。
[00:46.02]So he decided to emigrate. | 于是他决定移居他国。
[00:48.41]In the new country he became absorbed in making a new life for the two of us, so that he gradually ceased to grieve. | 在新的国家里，他一心为我们父子俩开创一种新的生活，渐渐地不再悲伤了。
[00:57.04]He did not marry again and I was brought up without a woman's care; but I lacked for nothing, for he was both father and mother to me. | 他没有再婚，我在没有母亲照料的情况下长大；但我什么都不缺，他既当爹又当妈。
[01:06.90]He always meant to go back one day, but not to stay. | 他一直打算有一天回去看看，但不是久住。
[01:10.65]His roots and mine had become too firmly embedded in the new land. | 他和我的根都已深深地扎在了新的国土上。
[01:15.54]But he wanted to see the old folk againand to visit my mother's grave. | 但他想再见见故乡的亲人，去看看母亲的坟墓。
[01:20.32]He became mortally ill a few months before we had planned to go and, when he knew that he was dying, he made me promise to go on my own. | 在我们计划启程的前几个月，他得了绝症。当他知道自己将不久于人世时，便让我答应独自回去一趟。
[01:31.44]I hired a car the day after landing and bought a comprehensive book of maps, | 着陆后的第二天，我租了一辆车，买了一本内容详尽的地图册，
[01:36.93]which I found most helpful on the cross-country journey, but which I did not think I should need on the last stage. | 在乡间的行车途中我发现它极为有用，但我认为在最后一段路程中用不着它。
[01:44.62]It was not that I actually remembered anything at all. | 这并不是说我真的记得什么。
[01:48.56]But my father had described over and over again what we should see at every milestone after leaving the nearest town, | 而是父亲曾一遍又一遍地告诉过我，离开最近的镇子之后，在每个里程碑处我们将看到什么，
[01:57.66]so that I was positive I should recognize it as familiar territory. | 所以我确信自己会把它当作熟悉的领地认出来。
[02:02.93]Well, I had been wrong, for I was now lost. | 唉，我错了，因为我此时迷了路。
[02:07.74]I looked at the map and then at the milometer. | 我看了看地图，又看了看里程表。
[02:11.33]I had come ten miles since leaving the town and at this point, according to my father, | 离开小镇以来我已走了10英里。按父亲的说法，在这个地方，
[02:18.39]I should be looking at farms and cottages in a valley, | 我应该俯瞰到山谷中的农舍和村舍，
[02:22.48]with the spire of the church of our village showing in the far distance. | 远方隐约显现出我们村里教堂的尖顶。
[02:27.63]I could see no valley, no farms, no cottages and no church spire-only a lake. | 可我看不到山谷、农舍、村舍和教堂尖顶——只有一个湖。
[02:34.88]I decided that I must have taken a wrong turning somewhere. | 我想肯定是在什么地方拐错了弯。
[02:39.19]So I drove back to the town and began to retrace the route, taking frequent glances at the map. | 于是我开车返回小镇，重新顺着路线走，不时看看地图。
[02:46.44]I landed up at the same corner. | 结果又来到了同一个路口。
[02:49.18]The curious thing was that the lake was not marked on the map. | 奇怪的是那个湖在地图上并没有标出来。
[02:53.27]I felt as if I had stumbled into a nightmare country, as you sometimes do in dreams. | 我觉得自己仿佛闯入了噩梦中的国度，就像你有时在梦中经历的那样。
[02:59.55]And, as in a nightmare, there was nobody in sight to help me. | 而且，就像在噩梦中一样，视野中没有人可以求助。
[03:04.43]Fortunately for me, as I was wondering what to do next, | 所幸的是，正当我不知所措时，
[03:08.52]there appeared on the horizon a man on horseback, riding in my direction. | 地平线上出现了一个骑马的人，朝我这个方向走来。
[03:14.01]I waited till he came near, then I asked him the way to our old village. | 我等他走近，然后向他打听我们老村的路径。
[03:19.45]He said that there was now no village. | 他说现在没有那个村庄了。
[03:22.51]I thought he must have misunderstood me, so I repeated its name. | 我以为他误解了我，便又说了一遍村名。
[03:28.08]This time he pointed to the lake. | 这一次他指了指湖。
[03:31.15]The village no longer existed because it had been submerged, and all the valley too. | 村庄已不复存在，因为它已被淹没在水下了，整个山谷也一样。
[03:38.49]The lake was not a natural one, but a man-made reservoir. | 那不是一个天然湖，而是一座人工水库。
